WEBVTT

00:06:59.626 --> 00:07:02.667
AG: Wherever you draw the line
on what counts as burnout,

00:07:02.691 --> 00:07:06.286
Annie and I agree
that it's not a pleasant place to be.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:08.726
You've probably felt this way before,

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.136
or maybe you feel burned out right now,

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:15.613
whether you work in retail
or manufacturing or public service,

00:07:15.637 --> 00:07:16.947
but you might be surprised

00:07:16.971 --> 00:07:20.272
that burnout is not necessarily
about how hard you work.

00:07:20.296 --> 00:07:21.753
(Music)

00:07:21.777 --> 00:07:25.309
Take it from an occupation
with one of the highest burnout rates,

00:07:25.333 --> 00:07:26.992
teaching.

00:07:27.016 --> 00:07:28.730
Conrey Callahan: I loved teaching.

00:07:28.754 --> 00:07:32.776
I was always involved in teaching
in lots of different ways.